WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:08.430
Jessica Alba is far from finished as an actress,
but we can't help noticing that we just aren't

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:10.709
seeing as much of her as we used to.

00:00:10.709 --> 00:00:14.330
While she seems to appear in a couple of movies
each year, her career has descended from the

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.820
high-profile heights of her superhero and
Dark Angel days.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.270
For a little while, in the wake of the first
couple Fantastic Four movies, it seemed like

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.770
she might've been done with showbiz for good.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:27.199
What was so bad behind the scenes that Alba
almost … disappeared?

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:28.550
The scripts sucked

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:32.730
Alba has suffered through more than her share
of serious critical busts, but the Fantastic

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:35.260
Four movies seemed to be the last straw.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:38.760
Venting about all the bad scripts she'd accepted
over the years, Alba told Elle:

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.159
"Good actors never use the script unless it's
amazing writing.

00:00:42.159 --> 00:00:45.210
All the good actors I've worked with, they
all say whatever they want to say."

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.479
The reaction to those comments was swift.

00:00:47.479 --> 00:00:51.100
Screenwriter John August took her to task
for her perceived rudeness, writing:

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:54.720
"Following your logic, you’ve never been
in a movie with both good actors and amazing

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:55.720
writing.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:59.229
That may be true, but it might hurt the feelings
of David Wain, Robert Rodriguez and Frank

00:00:59.229 --> 00:01:00.229
Miller."

00:01:00.229 --> 00:01:03.800
Still, it's telling that August failed to
mention Tim Story, director of the Fantastic

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.100
Four, either.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:09.070
Maybe even he recognized that maybe Alba might've
been justified in hating that one.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:10.830
And speaking of Tim Story...

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:13.390
They made her feel worthless

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:16.830
There can't be anything more demoralizing
for an actor than being asked not to do their

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:17.900
job.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:21.020
But that's exactly the sort of treatment Alba
says she received during the filming of the

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:23.550
widely panned Fantastic Four sequel.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:27.740
During one scene in Rise of the Silver Surfer,
Alba was supposed to be emotional.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:31.950
Director Tim Story reportedly berated her,
saying, "It looks too real, it looks too painful."

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:32.950
According to Alba:

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:35.040
"He was like, 'Don't do that thing with your
face.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.040
Just make it flat.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:37.200
We can CG the tears in.'

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.350
And so I just said, 'F— it.

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:40.620
I don't care about this business anymore.'"

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:42.350
The movies were ripped apart by critics

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:48.340
"An overinflated B-movie with no grace, no
subtext, no wit, and featuring beefcake/cheesecake

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:49.360
actors."

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.010
"Terribly miscast."

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:54.270
"The movie should almost be ashamed to show
itself."

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:56.070
There's no two ways about it.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:02:00.410
Far from fantastic, these movies were horribly
received, especially compared to genre contemporaries

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:02.360
like Spider-Man 2, Batman Begins, and X-Men.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:05.900
The reviews were particularly unkind to the
actors.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:09.769
Their performances were called thin, their
characters two-bit, and critics generally

00:02:09.769 --> 00:02:12.319
wrote off their hard work as a waste of time.

00:02:12.319 --> 00:02:16.130
That hurricane of hate would be enough to
make anybody doubt their career choices.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:19.790
For her part, Alba has shown a lot of self-awareness
when it comes to the quality of some of her

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:21.040
pictures, telling Elle:

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:24.390
"I know I haven't been swimming in the deep
end with some of the movies I've done.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:25.590
I wasn't trying to.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:26.590
I knew what they were.

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:29.280
I'd been so afraid of criticism ever since
I was young.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.470
Every time I'd get a critique or some redirection,
I'd always just take it very personally."

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:36.030
Is that any surprise she'd want to walk away?

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:37.080
Thanks for watching!

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.550
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw...

